# ManageMeals Web

SvelteKit frontend for [ManageMeals](https://managemeals.com) — a free recipe manager. Talks to a separate backend API (`manage-meals-api`).

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev              # Dev server
npm run build            # Production build
npm run check            # Type-check (svelte-check + tsc)
npm run lint             # Prettier + ESLint
npm run format           # Auto-format
npm run test:unit        # Vitest
npm run test:integration # Playwright E2E
```

## Tech stack

SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes), TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS 4 (via `src/app.css`), Axios (server-only), `@sveltejs/adapter-node`, Vitest + Playwright.

## Structure

- `src/routes/(app)/` — protected routes (auth required)
- `src/routes/(auth)/` — login, register, etc.
- `src/routes/(marketing)/` — public marketing pages
- `src/routes/infra/` — health checks
- `src/lib/components/` — reusable UI
- `src/lib/types.ts` — all shared interfaces
- `src/lib/server/api/client.ts` — Axios client factory
- `src/hooks.server.ts` — auth guard + token refresh

Dynamic routes use `[slug]/` (e.g. `recipes/[slug]/`).

## Principles

- Minimize scope — match existing patterns; don't over-engineer
- Server-only API calls — never call the backend from client code
- No commits unless explicitly requested
